# DIVE-2144, scope item 4. install.sh is the ONE file that survives the cutover as a
# mutable-main-to-root path: cmd_selfupdate.sh re-fetches it from raw main on EVERY
# upgrade and runs it as root via sudo bash. Publishing from a tag does not remove
# that risk, it CONCENTRATES it — one small file instead of a 47k-line bundle, which
# is a large improvement and also means a bad merge to this one path is still
# instantly live on every box. Gate it accordingly. (olivia's finding 4.)
#
# WHY @lodar AND NOT A TEAM: the first cut of this file said @5dive-ai/maintainers.
# That team does not exist — `gh api orgs/5dive-ai/teams` is empty and lodar is the
# repo's only collaborator. GitHub does not fail a CODEOWNERS entry naming a
# nonexistent team by refusing the merge; it just never requests the review. The file
# would have looked like a gate and been a no-op, which is the exact failure class
# this ticket exists to retire. Name a real owner or name none.
#
# CODEOWNERS only REQUESTS review on its own. It becomes a REQUIRED approval when
# "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in main's branch protection — a
# repo-admin setting this file cannot set and does not claim to have set.
#
# DIVE-4334, 2026-09-12 — THE CONTROL IS UNCHANGED; THE ATTESTER MOVED.
# Everything above still holds: a required, attributable human-class review on the
# one mutable-main-to-root path. What changed is WHO signs it. Routing every
# installer PR to @lodar made a graded-PASS, green, CTO-cleared ship wait on a
# person (measured: PR #880 held ~1h on this line, #885 behind it), and he does not
# want the ping. So the owner is now a dedicated login that the ship rail can sign
# as, and the taps stop.
#
# WHY THIS LOGIN AND NOT AN EXISTING ONE — the owner needs four properties and the
# other two accounts each fail one: CODEOWNERS resolves USERS and TEAMS only (so
# the GitHub App identity can never be named here, whatever its repo permissions),
# and GitHub 422s a self-approval (so it cannot be @5dive-bot, which authors every
# installer PR). @5dive-reviewer is a user, holds write, is not the author, and its
# credential is reachable only through `5dive gh --as=reviewer`, a root-side rail
# allowlisted to `pr review` — it signs, it does not work.
#
# WHAT THE REVIEW ATTESTS, and this is the part a reader should hold us to: the
# automated rail at the head being approved — docker-install, test-installed-host
# (+confirm), supply-chain-guard, shellcheck, scan — plus the verifier's PASS and
# the CTO clearance named in the review body. A human eye on the diff is NOT what
# it attests any more. That is the residual this change signs for; it is recorded
# on DIVE-4334 rather than implied here.
/install.sh            @5dive-reviewer
/src/cmd_selfupdate.sh @5dive-reviewer
